# A custom .stow-local-ignore REPLACES stow's built-in default ignore list, so we
# must re-list the defaults we still want alongside our own additions — otherwise
# stow would start symlinking README.md into $HOME. Same reasoning as the
# chime and voice-pipeline packages.

# --- our additions ---
# .gitconfig is deliberately NOT stowed. `git config --global` writes to
# ~/.gitconfig whenever that file exists, and `gh auth setup-git` (also the
# "Authenticate Git with your GitHub credentials?" step of `gh auth login`) uses
# exactly that to install its credential helper. With ~/.gitconfig symlinked
# into this repo, those writes land in the working tree and show up as an
# unexplained dirty file after an unrelated push.
#
# Instead, install.sh writes a small per-machine ~/.gitconfig that [include]s
# this file. Tool writes land in that untracked shim; the tracked config is
# never touched. The per-OS .gitconfig-{linux,macos,windows} files below are
# still stowed normally — only the shared entry point is special.
^/\.gitconfig$

# --- stow's usual defaults, restated ---
^/README.*
^/LICENSE.*
^/COPYING
\.gitignore$
\.git$
\.gitmodules$
\.DS_Store$
